  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a commit-addressed **`sha-\u003ccommit\u003e`** image alias to `docker-build-check`, pointing at the same content-fingerprinted manifest the run-scoped lookup tag already aliases.\n\nThis is the producer side of [romaine-life/glimmung#873](https://github.com/romaine-life/glimmung/pull/873), which re-keys the test-slot deploy-image resolver from CI-run identity to **commit identity** — looking the image up by the verified commit SHA directly instead of reconstructing a `ci-pr`/`ci-ref` lookup tag from GitHub Actions run metadata (the source of the 2026-06-20 deploy-image race).\n\n**Additive and safe:** the existing run-scoped lookup tag is unchanged, so nothing breaks before or after glimmung#873 merges. Once the resolver reads `sha-\u003ccommit\u003e`, a follow-up removes the now-dead lookup tag.\n\n**Merge order:** merge this *before* glimmung#873 so the alias is published before the resolver switches to reading it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
  "changed_files": 1,
